.Dd
.Dt COMA 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm coma
.Nd a keyboard driven, tiling terminal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar config
.Op Fl l Ar layout
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a keyboard driven tiling terminal. It opens a single window in which
it runs shells, laid out in frames. By default
.Nm
will attempt to create 484 pixel frames in its window.
.Pp
These defaults can be overwritten using the configuration file.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The configuration file by default exists in
.An $HOME/.comarc
but can be given
on the command line with the
.Op Fl c
flag.
.Pp
The following options can be configured:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic font (default: fixed:pixelsize=13:style=bold)
The font to be used by coma for status bars and input.
.It Ic frame-layout (default: default)
Change frame layout. options: default, small-large, small-dual.
The layout can also be given on the command line with the
.Op Fl l
flag.
.It Ic frame-gap (default: 20)
The gap between frames and from the top and bottom of the screen.
.It Ic frame-bar (default: 35)
The height of the bar at the bottom of the frames.
.It Ic frame-border (default: 5)
The width of the border around frames and their bars.
.It Ic frame-count (default: auto).
The number of frames to create (by default
.Nm
will create frames until they no longer fit on-screen).
.It Ic frame-width (default: 484)
The width of each frame.
.It Ic frame-height (default: fill)
The height of each frame.
.It Ic frame-offset (default: centered)
The X offset where you want things to be created from.
.It Ic screen-width (default: display width)
The initial width of the
.Nm
window.
.It Ic screen-height (default: display height)
The initial height of the
.Nm
window.
.It Ic window-decorations (default: no)
Set to yes to let the window manager draw its title bar and borders
around the
.Nm
window.
.It Ic shell (default: $SHELL)
The program started in new terminals.
.It Ic terminal-font (default: monospace:pixelsize=13)
The font used in terminals, either a fontconfig name or a path to
a font file optionally followed by :size (eg: ~/fonts/font.pcf:14).
.It Ic terminal-font-bold (default: none)
The font used for bold text in terminals, same format as terminal-font.
When not set, bold is synthesized from terminal-font.
.It Ic terminal-name (default: xterm-256color)
The value of TERM in terminals.
.It Ic scrollback (default: 2000)
The number of lines kept in the scrollback of each terminal.
.It Ic terminal
Ignored, accepted for compatibility with older configurations.
.It Ic bind
Bind the given key to the action specified. (see key bindings below).
If the action is prefixed with cmd_shell: the keybinding will run that
command outside of coma instead, the command may have arguments (use
double quotes for arguments with spaces) and the key is always last.
.Pp
Example: bind frame-next p
.Pp
Example: bind cmd_shell:firefox --private-window f
.It Ic color
Set the color for the specified type (see colors below).
.Pp
Example: color client-active "#55007a"
.It Ic prefix (default: C-t)
Configure the prefix key. The format of this key is in the form of MOD-KEY.
.Pp
Allowed MODs: C (Control), S (Shift), M (mod1), M2 (mod2), M3 (mod3), M4 (mod4).
.El
.Sh KEY BINDINGS
All key bindings start with the prefix key which by default is
.Ic C\-t .
The prefix key can be configured in the
.An configuration file .
.Pp
These are the default key bindings for all actions:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic C\-t C\-t
Send the prefix key itself to the terminal
.It Ic C\-t c (coma-terminal)
Start a new terminal in the current frame
.It Ic C\-t v (coma-terminal-secure)
Start a new terminal in the current frame that is sandboxed from the internet.
.It Ic C\-t h (frame-prev)
Move to the previous frame
.It Ic C\-t l (frame-next)
Move to the next frame
.It Ic C\-t z (frame-zoom)
Zoom/unzoom the current frame
.It Ic C\-t s (frame-split)
Split the current frame vertically (can be done only once)
.It Ic C\-t m (frame-merge)
Merge a vertically split frame back together into one
.It Ic C\-t f (frame-split-next)
Toggle between the upper and lower part of a vertical split
.It Ic C\-t w (frame-layout-swap)
Swap the frame layout, followed by 1 (default), 2 (small-large)
or 3 (small-dual)
.It Ic C\-t 1-9
Move to the frame with that number
.It Ic C\-t i (frame-move-client-left)
Move the active client to the left
.It Ic C\-t o (frame-move-client-right)
Move the active client to the right
.It Ic C\-t q (coma-client-list)
Display client quick selection list
.It Ic C\-t k (client-kill)
Kill the active client (no warning will be presented)
.It Ic C\-t p (client-prev)
Swap to the previous client in the frame
.It Ic C\-t n (client-next)
Swap to the next client in the frame
.It Ic C\-t colon (coma-command)
Runs an internal WM command,
.Ic tag Ar name
sets the name shown for the active client and
.Ic untag
removes it again
.El
.Sh COLORS
Colors must be in RGB format prefixed with a pound character and
quoted in double quotes:
.Pp
color client-active "#ffffff"
.Pp
The following colors can be configured:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic client-active
The border color for the current active client.
.It Ic client-inactive
The border color for inactive clients.
.It Ic frame-bar
The color for the frame bars.
.It Ic frame-bar-inactive
The color for the frame bars of inactive frames.
.It Ic frame-bar-directory
The directory path of the active client.
.It Ic frame-bar-client-active
The text color for the active client in the frame bar.
.It Ic frame-bar-client-inactive
The text color for the inactive client in the frame bar.
.It Ic command-input
The text color of the command prompt and client list.
.It Ic command-bar
The background color of the command prompt and client list.
.It Ic command-border
The border color of the command prompt and client list.
.It Ic background
The window background behind the frames.
.It Ic terminal-foreground
The default text color in terminals.
.It Ic terminal-background
The default background color in terminals.
.El
.Sh MOUSE
Selecting text with the left button copies it to the primary selection,
a double click selects a word and a triple click a line.
The middle button and Shift-Insert paste the primary selection.
The scroll wheel and Shift-PageUp / Shift-PageDown scroll back.
Hold Shift to select text in programs that use the mouse.
.Sh AUTHORS
.Nm
